```
  Exported with external C linkage and declared in the retained
  `pjmedia/include/pjmedia/rtp.h`; a required symbol of the libpjmedia
  archive. Reached through the retained same-file wrapper
  `pjmedia_rtp_decode_rtp`, which forwards all arguments and supplies its own
  local `pjmedia_rtp_dec_hdr`, and called directly by external programs that
  link the archive.
- **Observable behavior:** Decodes a raw RTP packet into header, optional
  extension header, and payload. All outputs point inside the caller'"'"'s packet
  buffer; header fields remain in network byte order; the session argument is
  unused and no session state is read or written.
- **Inputs:** `pkt`/`pkt_len` — the packet bytes and their byte count;
  `hdr`, `dec_hdr`, `payload`, `payloadlen` — caller-owned outputs.
- **Outputs and errors:** Returns PJMEDIA_RTP_EINVER when the header version
  field differs from RTP_VERSION (2); PJMEDIA_RTP_EINLEN when the computed
  header extent exceeds `pkt_len`; otherwise PJ_SUCCESS. `*hdr` is set to the
  packet start before the version outcome. The offset starts at
  sizeof(pjmedia_rtp_hdr) (12) plus one 32-bit word per CSRC (`cc`). When the
  extension bit `x` is set: `dec_hdr->ext_hdr` points at the extension header
  at that offset inside the packet, `dec_hdr->ext` points immediately past
  it, `dec_hdr->ext_len` is the extension header'"'"'s 16-bit length field
  converted from network order (a count of 32-bit words), and the offset
  advances by (ext_len+1)*4 bytes; otherwise the three members become
  NULL/NULL/0. Only on the
  success path: `*payload` is the packet byte at the offset and `*payloadlen`
  is pkt_len minus offset; when the padding bit `p` is set and the payload is
  non-empty, the payload'"'"'s final byte is taken as a padding count and, when
  not greater than the payload length, reduces `*payloadlen`.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Writes only the caller-owned outputs;
  reads no global or session state.
- **Required sequencing and state:** Stateless; no ordering requirements
  between calls.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained: the range spans one complete PJ_DEF
  function definition. The retained text immediately above ends with the
  closing brace of `pjmedia_rtp_decode_rtp` and the retained text immediately
