    through /app/go.mod and the pre-downloaded module cache; dependencies not
    already required by go.mod cannot be fetched or added when the
    measurement runs, and go.mod is not rewritable in this mode.
  - Before every run the caller deletes, if present: /app/vendor, /app/go.work,
    any go.mod or go.work inside the package directory, and every *_test.go
    file in /app/pkg/webhook/ownerreference except its own staged probe.
    Implementation code must therefore live in regular (non-_test) source
    files of the package.
  - The staged probe is an external test package, so only exported
    identifiers of `package ownerreference` are reachable from it.

## Test harness boundary
  The calling side is a pytest driver plus a shared Python plumbing module
  that stages the Go probe into the package directory, launches `go test`
  with the sanitized environment above, and parses the go test output lines;
  the Go probe file itself is caller-owned and is re-copied over its staged
  location on every run. The probe'"'"'s in-memory client.Client, its
  configuration.Configuration stub, its event recorder, and the
  admission.Request values it constructs all belong to the calling side.
  None of this is part of the implementation: do not rebuild, replace, or
  modify any of it. Everything inside
  /app/pkg/webhook/ownerreference except the staged probe, plus the rest of
  the /app module it links against, is what the implementation owns.
